# November 24, 2026: a third scatter across Alabama, still the state with the fewest places on the map (47).
# Ground claimed with tools/choose.py --thinnest (al). Eleven places, spread from the Gulf coast (Fort Morgan, Fort Gaines,
# two Mobile houses) through Montgomery and Tuskegee to Tuscaloosa, Birmingham and the Tennessee Valley (Huntsville,
# Tuscumbia). Nothing that tools/start.py listed was repeated.
# Sources read in this session: Wikipedia (tools/wiki_raw.py); the Encyclopedia of Alabama; the Alabama Historical
# Commission's plan-your-visit page (Fort Morgan); the Town of Dauphin Island's Fort Gaines page; the National Park
# Service's Tuskegee pages; the pages of Ivy Green, Bragg-Mitchell Mansion, 16th Street Baptist Church, Rickwood Field and
# the Gorgas House Museum. Read with tools/page.py.
